{
  "schema": "northstar-stage3-handoff-results-v1",
  "status": "PassedLimitedPreparedRouteAndQueueHandoffSlice",
  "scope": [
    "The actual private XML preparation, mode-aware continuation, existing DirectMessageRouter and real OutboundSender share an operation-bound, single-use handoff. A local queue acceptance is recorded synchronously at the real sender result.",
    "Routing requires actual Stored with known returned Live mode and the existing finalization-attempt boundary. Replay, unknown returned mode and SpoolOnly do not acquire live routing authority.",
    "Prepared source, canonical full/bare target and fallback, health enforcement, live payload and exact durable item are validated before enqueue. A refused item remains intact across primary/fallback; durable Full still latches disconnect.",
    "Remote no-positive-receipt history survives later acceptance. Rearm records entered/returned attempts only; it does not claim a SQL release receipt. First route terminal facts are monotone.",
    "Queue acceptance survives a synthetic later pending continuation drop. This does not assert that the production router suspends after its local-success short-circuit."
  ],
